# Verifying a sender (identity.VerifySender) — one walk from a signing key down to
# the member root it belongs to. A missing link is "fetch and retry"; a bad sig,
# expiry, or revocation is terminal.
#
# v2: there is NO trusted-root check here. VerifySender RESOLVES identity; it does
# not decide trust, and admission to a relay is a separate, operational gate.
direction: down

start: "sender_pub\n(session OR device key)" { shape: oval; style.fill: "#fefce8" }
sess: "session_delegation?\nresolve session → device" { shape: diamond; style.fill: "#f1f5f9" }
walk: "walk device tree:\ndevice → device_delegation → parent …\n(≤ MaxChainDepth 8, cycle-checked)" { style.fill: "#eff6ff" }
revoke: "revocation check at EVERY hop\n(revoke binds only from an ancestor)" { style.fill: "#fef2f2"; style.stroke: "#b91c1c" }
att: "member root → SELF-signed\nidentity_attestation" { style.fill: "#ecfdf5" }
ok: "RESOLVED\n{ member_pub, kind, operated_by, display_name }" { shape: oval; style.fill: "#dcfce7"; style.stroke: "#15803d" }
bad: "REJECT\nErrRevoked / ErrExpired / ErrBadSignature\nErrChainTooDeep / ErrChainCycle" { shape: oval; style.fill: "#fee2e2"; style.stroke: "#b91c1c" }
fetch: "ErrUnknownObject\n→ GetIdentityObject(hash), retry" { style.fill: "#fff7ed"; style.stroke: "#c2410c" }

start -> sess
sess -> walk: "device key"
walk -> revoke -> att
att -> ok: "self-signature verifies"
att -> bad: "bad self-sig / pubkey mismatch"
revoke -> bad: "revoked / expired"
walk -> fetch: "link missing"
att -> fetch: "attestation missing"

gate: |md
  **Resolution is not admission.** `RESOLVED` only means *"this key provably belongs
  to member M, who claims this profile."* Two further, independent decisions follow:

  - **Operational — may M use this relay?** The allow-list gate
    (`core.enforceAccess`): an **open** relay auto-admits and records the member
    trust-on-first-use; an **invite-only** relay rejects with `ErrNotAllowed`
    until an invite is redeemed.
  - **Trust — should *you* believe M is who they claim?** An **edge** decision:
    pairing, a shared room, or the relay directory. Never the chain's answer.
| { near: bottom-center; style.font-size: 13 }
